  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "B3_NULL_AUTHORIZATION_BYPASS_NOT_FAIL_CLOSED",
      "severity": "P1",
      "status": "open",
      "affectedPaths": [
        "supabase/migrations/20260730161737_allow_room_host_participant_block_check.sql",
        "supabase/tests/room_host_participant_block_check_test.sql",
        "docs/assurance/reconciliation/b3-room-host-block-check.json"
      ],
      "evidence": "The function authorizes only inside `if v_auth_user_id is not null and v_auth_user_id <> v_actor_user_id` at migration lines 26-37. A null auth.uid() skips both the self check and exact-room-host check, then the SECURITY DEFINER query at lines 39-47 evaluates any supplied actor. EXECUTE is granted to authenticated and service_role at lines 53-55. The pgTAP file sets three non-null subject claims but never exercises a null subject or distinguishes authenticated from the deliberate service-role path.",
      "impact": "The database authority boundary relies on every authenticated execution having a non-null JWT subject. If that assumption is violated, an authenticated execution can inspect block state for an arbitrary actor through an RLS-bypassing function. The reported T3 security result therefore is not fail-closed proof.",
      "requiredResolution": "Do not rewrite the deployed migration. Add a separately reviewed forward-only correction that rejects null identity for authenticated execution while preserving only an explicitly justified service-role path. Add real role-context pgTAP cases for authenticated null-sub rejection and the intended service-role null-sub behavior, then update the reconciliation report at the new exact head."
    },
    {
      "id": "B3_SECURITY_DEFINER_SEARCH_PATH_HARDENING_UNPROVED",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "open",
      "affectedPaths": [
        "supabase/migrations/20260730161737_allow_room_host_participant_block_check.sql",
        "supabase/tests/room_host_participant_block_check_test.sql"
      ],
      "evidence": "The function is SECURITY DEFINER with `set search_path = public`, and the test asserts that value. Relations and auth.uid() are schema-qualified, which reduces exposure, but this PR contains no assertion that untrusted roles cannot CREATE in public and does not use an empty search_path.",
      "impact": "No name-shadowing exploit is demonstrated, but the privileged function's search-path safety depends on an unproved schema privilege outside this three-file delta.",
      "requiredResolution": "Preserve the deployed file byte-for-byte. In the forward-only security correction, prefer an empty search_path with every object schema-qualified, or add authoritative schema-CREATE denial evidence and a regression assertion."
    },
    {
      "id": "B3_PGTAP_AUTHORITY_MATRIX_INCOMPLETE",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "open",
      "affectedPaths": [
        "supabase/tests/room_host_participant_block_check_test.sql"
      ],
      "evidence": "The 10 assertions cover function metadata, catalog grants, participant self, exact host, blocked/unblocked, and one unrelated non-host. They do not SET ROLE, test null/empty arguments, test a host against another host's room, or execute the service-role and anonymous boundaries.",
      "impact": "The suite demonstrates the principal happy and denial paths but does not cover every authority branch named by the function contract.",
      "requiredResolution": "Extend the focused pgTAP matrix with application-role calls, authenticated null-sub denial, deliberate service-role behavior, invalid argument behavior, and an exact-room cross-host denial. Keep provider and remote access out of the test."
    },
    {
      "id": "B3_EXACT_DEPLOYED_MIGRATION_IDENTITY",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "resolution": "The added file uses deployed version 20260730161737 and name allow_room_host_participant_block_check. Its raw SHA-256 equals the preserved read-only remote statement-array hash."
    },
    {
      "id": "B3_DUPLICATE_MIGRATION_APPLICATION",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "resolution": "The earlier source copy and exact remote file differ only by the final newline. CREATE OR REPLACE plus repeated revoke/grant is statement-idempotent, and the implementation report records both versions applying in order with no duplicate-object error or semantic drift."
    },
    {
      "id": "B3_GRANT_AND_RLS_NET_CHANGE",
      "severity": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "resolution": "The delta changes no table grant, policy, RLS, or FORCE RLS setting. It revokes PUBLIC function execution and restores the pre-existing authenticated/service_role function grants; reported pgTAP confirms anon denial."
    }
  ],
